# Kconfig symbols introduced by OUR patches in target/linux/qualcommax/patches-*.
#
# Those patches apply to every subtarget of qualcommax, so each symbol has to
# be answered in the SHARED config-<version>, not only in ipq50xx/config-default.
# Otherwise a build of ipq807x/ipq60xx meets a new, visible, unanswered symbol
# during syncconfig, kconfig turns interactive and dies on EOF. Our own CI only
# builds ipq50xx and cannot see it - this list is how we catch it anyway.
#
# The shared entry is "# CONFIG_X is not set"; ipq50xx/config-default overrides
# it to =y where the symbol is actually wanted.
#
# Note this only bites symbols with no unmet dependency: upstream's
# REGULATOR_CPR3_NPU and friends are unanswered for ipq50xx too, but they are
# invisible there, so kconfig never asks. Ours have no depends and are always
# visible - hence this list, rather than a blanket scan of every patch.
#
# Add a line here whenever a patch of ours introduces a new symbol.

PCS_QCA_UNIPHY
DWMAC_IPQ5018
PHY_QCOM_IPQ5018_USB_SS
